    <licenseUrl>https://github.com/narcisbodea/smstunnel-cli/blob/main/LICENSE</licenseUrl>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <projectSourceUrl>https://github.com/narcisbodea/smstunnel-cli</projectSourceUrl>
    <docsUrl>https://smstunnel.io/docs/</docsUrl>
    <bugTrackerUrl>https://github.com/narcisbodea/smstunnel-cli/issues</bugTrackerUrl>
    <tags>smstunnel sms text-message android cli command-line sign-in-code</tags>
    <summary>Send texts from your computer through your own Android phone and number</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[The `smstunnel` command sends texts from your computer through your own Android phone, from your own number.

Your phone runs the [SMSTunnel app from Google Play](https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=io.smstunnel.app) and sends each text from its own SIM, so people see a number they know and can reply to it. The command also sends sign-in codes, checks whether a text went out, lists the texts your phone received and shows what is left of your plan today.

## Get started

1. Install the SMSTunnel app on your Android phone and sign in.
2. In your dashboard, [dashboard.smstunnel.io/apps](https://dashboard.smstunnel.io/apps), open **Apps → Add an app** and copy the key.
3. Run `smstunnel login` and paste the key (it is saved in Windows Credential Manager), then `smstunnel send +40712345678 "Hello"`.

One number per text. Documentation: [smstunnel.io/docs](https://smstunnel.io/docs/).

SMSTunnel is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Chocolatey or Microsoft.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/narcisbodea/smstunnel-cli/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
